{
  "$schema": "https://schema.management.azure.com/schemas/2019-04-01/deploymentTemplate.json#",
  "contentVersion": "1.0.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "comments": [
      "Holds the stopwatch for the weekly load, and raises the alarm when the",
      "load does not happen. The chain itself stays on GitHub Actions: this",
      "posts a workflow_dispatch, waits, asks what became of it, and writes to",
      "a mailbox if the answer is not 'success'.",
      "",
      "Why it exists: GitHub does not promise to run a schedule, and both real",
      "firings were late — 110 minutes on 10 Sep 2026 and 144 on 16 Sep. A Logic",
      "App recurrence has an SLA and carries a Windows time zone, so 09:07 stays",
      "09:07 across daylight saving.",
      "",
      "Why it also watches: weekly.yml has no schedule behind this trigger",
      "(19 Sep 2026). Nothing else would notice a dispatch that did not happen,",
      "so the trigger has to notice itself.",
      "",
      "Deploying it is docs/ci_setup.md, step 7. The token is a securestring:",
      "it is not written to the deployment history, the workflow definition",
      "returns it masked, and secureData hides the run inputs that carry it."
    ]
  },
  "parameters": {
    "workflowName": {
      "type": "string",
      "defaultValue": "trigger-weekly-load"
    },
    "connectionName": {
      "type": "string",
      "defaultValue": "outlook-mail"
    },
    "location": {
      "type": "string",
      "defaultValue": "australiaeast"
    },
    "repository": {
      "type": "string",
      "defaultValue": "AndRayFS/nz-fuel-price-azure-fabric"
    },
    "ref": {
      "type": "string",
      "defaultValue": "main",
      "metadata": {
        "description": "The federated credential names refs/heads/main, so a dispatch on any other ref fails at azure/login."
      }
    },
    "alertTo": {
      "type": "string",
      "defaultValue": "morozov_77@hotmail.com",
      "metadata": {
        "description": "The mailbox that already carries the budget alerts and is read daily."
      }
    },
    "waitMinutes": {
      "type": "int",
      "defaultValue": 60,
      "metadata": {
        "description": "Longer than weekly.yml's own timeout-minutes: 45, so the run has certainly concluded before it is asked about."
      }
    },
    "githubToken": {
      "type": "securestring",
      "metadata": {
        "description": "Fine-grained PAT on this repository alone, permission Actions: read and write. Its expiry is a dated item in .claude/rules/active-items.md."
      }
    }
  },
  "resources": [
    {
      "type": "Microsoft.Web/connections",
      "apiVersion": "2016-06-01",
      "name": "[parameters('connectionName')]",
      "location": "[parameters('location')]",
      "properties": {
        "displayName": "[parameters('alertTo')]",
        "api": {
          "id": "[subscriptionResourceId('Microsoft.Web/locations/managedApis', parameters('location'), 'outlook')]"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "Microsoft.Logic/workflows",
      "apiVersion": "2019-05-01",
      "name": "[parameters('workflowName')]",
      "location": "[parameters('location')]",
      "dependsOn": [
        "[resourceId('Microsoft.Web/connections', parameters('connectionName'))]"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "state": "Enabled",
        "definition": {
          "$schema": "https://schema.management.azure.com/providers/Microsoft.Logic/schemas/2016-06-01/workflowdefinition.json#",
          "contentVersion": "1.0.0.0",
          "parameters": {
            "$connections": {
              "type": "Object",
              "defaultValue": {}
            },
            "githubToken": {
              "type": "securestring"
            },
            "dispatchUri": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "runsUri": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "ref": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "alertTo": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "waitMinutes": {
              "type": "int"
            }
          },
          "triggers": {
            "Recurrence": {
              "type": "Recurrence",
              "recurrence": {
                "frequency": "Week",
                "interval": 1,
                "timeZone": "New Zealand Standard Time",
                "startTime": "2026-09-24T09:07:00",
                "schedule": {
                  "weekDays": [
                    "Thursday"
                  ],
                  "hours": [
                    9
                  ],
                  "minutes": [
                    7
                  ]
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "actions": {
            "Dispatch_the_weekly_load": {
              "type": "Http",
              "runAfter": {},
              "inputs": {
                "method": "POST",
                "uri": "@parameters('dispatchUri')",
                "headers": {
                  "Accept": "application/vnd.github+json",
                  "Authorization": "Bearer @{parameters('githubToken')}",
                  "User-Agent": "nz-fuel-price-trigger-weekly-load",
                  "X-GitHub-Api-Version": "2022-11-28"
                },
                "body": {
                  "ref": "@parameters('ref')"
                }
              },
              "runtimeConfiguration": {
                "secureData": {
                  "properties": [
                    "inputs"
                  ]
                }
              }
            },
            "Wait_for_the_load_to_finish": {
              "type": "Wait",
              "description": "Every outcome of the dispatch leads here, a failed POST included: a token that has expired is exactly the case the alarm exists for, and it must not stop the alarm from being raised.",
              "runAfter": {
                "Dispatch_the_weekly_load": [
                  "Succeeded",
                  "Failed",
                  "Skipped",
                  "TimedOut"
                ]
              },
              "inputs": {
                "interval": {
                  "count": "@parameters('waitMinutes')",
                  "unit": "Minute"
                }
              }
            },
            "Ask_GitHub_what_happened": {
              "type": "Http",
              "runAfter": {
                "Wait_for_the_load_to_finish": [
                  "Succeeded"
                ]
              },
              "inputs": {
                "method": "GET",
                "uri": "@parameters('runsUri')",
                "headers": {
                  "Accept": "application/vnd.github+json",
                  "Authorization": "Bearer @{parameters('githubToken')}",
                  "User-Agent": "nz-fuel-price-trigger-weekly-load",
                  "X-GitHub-Api-Version": "2022-11-28"
                }
              },
              "runtimeConfiguration": {
                "secureData": {
                  "properties": [
                    "inputs"
                  ]
                }
              }
            },
            "Did_the_load_go_through": {
              "type": "If",
              "description": "Two questions, not one. A run that concluded 'success' but was created last week means this week's dispatch never produced one, so the age is as load-bearing as the conclusion. first() returns null on an empty list rather than failing, which is why the list is never indexed.",
              "runAfter": {
                "Ask_GitHub_what_happened": [
                  "Succeeded"
                ]
              },
              "expression": {
                "and": [
                  {
                    "equals": [
                      "@coalesce(first(body('Ask_GitHub_what_happened')?['workflow_runs'])?['conclusion'], 'no run at all')",
                      "success"
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "greater": [
                      "@ticks(coalesce(first(body('Ask_GitHub_what_happened')?['workflow_runs'])?['created_at'], '1970-01-01T00:00:00Z'))",
                      "@ticks(addHours(utcNow(), -3))"
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              "actions": {},
              "else": {
                "actions": {
                  "Say_the_load_did_not_go_through": {
                    "type": "ApiConnection",
                    "inputs": {
                      "host": {
                        "connection": {
                          "name": "@parameters('$connections')['outlook']['connectionId']"
                        }
                      },
                      "method": "post",
                      "path": "/v2/Mail",
                      "body": {
                        "To": "@parameters('alertTo')",
                        "Subject": "NZ fuel price: the weekly load did not go through",
                        "Importance": "Normal",
                        "Body": "<p>The trigger fired and the load did not reach a good end.</p><p>Newest dispatched run: conclusion <b>@{coalesce(first(body('Ask_GitHub_what_happened')?['workflow_runs'])?['conclusion'], 'no run at all')}</b>, created @{coalesce(first(body('Ask_GitHub_what_happened')?['workflow_runs'])?['created_at'], '—')}.</p><p><a href=\"@{coalesce(first(body('Ask_GitHub_what_happened')?['workflow_runs'])?['html_url'], 'https://github.com/AndRayFS/nz-fuel-price-azure-fabric/actions')}\">Open it in Actions</a></p><p>No run at all, or one older than three hours, means the dispatch never landed — read this Logic App's run history. A conclusion of failure means the chain broke, and the run's own log says where.</p>"
                      }
                    }
                  }
                }
              }
            },
            "Say_GitHub_could_not_be_asked": {
              "type": "ApiConnection",
              "description": "The alarm shares a credential with the thing it watches, so the case where the question itself cannot be asked gets its own mail rather than silence.",
              "runAfter": {
                "Ask_GitHub_what_happened": [
                  "Failed",
                  "TimedOut"
                ]
              },
              "inputs": {
                "host": {
                  "connection": {
                    "name": "@parameters('$connections')['outlook']['connectionId']"
                  }
                },
                "method": "post",
                "path": "/v2/Mail",
                "body": {
                  "To": "@parameters('alertTo')",
                  "Subject": "NZ fuel price: cannot tell whether the weekly load ran",
                  "Importance": "Normal",
                  "Body": "<p>The dispatch was sent, but GitHub could not be asked what became of it: the call to the runs API did not succeed.</p><p>A 401 there means the fine-grained PAT has expired or been revoked, which also means the dispatch itself did not land. Check the load by hand.</p>"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "outputs": {}
        },
        "parameters": {
          "$connections": {
            "value": {
              "outlook": {
                "connectionId": "[resourceId('Microsoft.Web/connections', parameters('connectionName'))]",
                "connectionName": "[parameters('connectionName')]",
                "id": "[subscriptionResourceId('Microsoft.Web/locations/managedApis', parameters('location'), 'outlook')]"
              }
            }
          },
          "githubToken": {
            "value": "[parameters('githubToken')]"
          },
          "dispatchUri": {
            "value": "[format('https://api.github.com/repos/{0}/actions/workflows/weekly.yml/dispatches', parameters('repository'))]"
          },
          "runsUri": {
            "value": "[format('https://api.github.com/repos/{0}/actions/workflows/weekly.yml/runs?event=workflow_dispatch&per_page=1', parameters('repository'))]"
          },
          "ref": {
            "value": "[parameters('ref')]"
          },
          "alertTo": {
            "value": "[parameters('alertTo')]"
          },
          "waitMinutes": {
            "value": "[parameters('waitMinutes')]"
          }
        }
      }
    }
  ],
  "outputs": {
    "workflowName": {
      "type": "string",
      "value": "[parameters('workflowName')]"
    },
    "connectionNeedsAuthorising": {
      "type": "string",
      "value": "[format('Open {0} in the portal and authorise it as {1} before the first Thursday.', parameters('connectionName'), parameters('alertTo'))]"
    }
  }
}
